    5. For each sprite, randomly remove 7-33% of template ON-pixels to create a damaged copy; ensure the union of all damaged copies still covers every template pixel (repair any uncovered pixel by restoring it in a random sprite that had it removed)
    6. Write damaged sprites into input grid at their window positions; output grid gets full template at each window
